    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bluefield grew from a tiny post office called Pin Hook in the 1860s, named after a creek that ran through the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluefield%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When coal was found, a railroad to the Pocahontas Coalfields was built and the town was renamed Graham to honor a Philadelphia capitalist.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluefield%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic downtown district, built mainly between 1895 and 1920, showcases Reconstruction and post‑WWI architectural styles.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.dhr.virginia.gov/historic-registers/143-5083/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Tourists can visit the Sanders House and the Bailey Log House, two preserved homes that highlight Bluefield’s coal‑era heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
